.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
setdev
- show or set a Micronix kernel's root and swap devices
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
setdev kernel [ root swap ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Setdev reads the symbol table of a Micronix kernel and prints or
changes the _rootdev and _swapdev words in it.  With no devices it
prints them; with two it writes them.
.sp
A device is written either as major/minor - 3/0 - or as a plain
number, decimal or 0x hex, so 3/0, 0x300 and 768 all agree.
.sp
This replaces the old ddt recipe, which searched the kernel for the
bytes of the root device it expected to find.  The kernel carries a
symbol table, so _rootdev and _swapdev say where they are, and nothing
has to be guessed.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
